This is a core work package. Start only after the named providers publish verified native/backend/persistence contracts and the package's implementation scope is authorized. Do not wait for an entire former numbered stage unless that contract acceptance is explicitly listed above. Do not use an unfinished sibling or mocked replacement as a hidden prerequisite.

## Delivered boundary

Bounded supplied character customization, first/third-person controls, attachments and nonphysical shared presence in a standalone room.

## Ownership and possible overlap

Character presentation/controller adapters and appearance tools; use stable shared asset and controller services.

Independent ready packages may proceed together only after file/service ownership is reserved. Use separate leaf modules or isolated checkouts; shared migrations, command schemas, source/selection types, renderer lifetimes, runtime scheduling and performance sessions have one owner at a time. If actual code inspection finds an unproved shared boundary, add a dependency or serialize that work before coding. No promised worker count follows from the graph.

## Ordered work

Follow this package's task order. Original identifiers remain traceable; a reference to another former stage means its needed published contract, not an implicit global sequence. All native interaction, backend/persistence, authority, correctness and applicable resource obligations remain included.

### Task 05.T14

- [ ] **05.T14.** Extend the existing navigation/presence family with the B41 starter subset: explicit controlled occurrence, first/third-person follow settings, source-defined forward/up/eye/foot anchors, bounded speed/acceleration/turn/step/slope settings and standing/walking presentation where supplied clips support it. Resolve camera obstruction against ready permitted geometry; keep body movement and camera placement separately owned. Free Fly changes the view unless an explicit supported body-control profile is selected. Use the existing query-based controller, offline loader and bounded presence transport; no new joint dynamics, clinical anatomy or mandatory participant collider. Missing required support reconciles visibly, and missing optional appearance uses a cheap fallback.

### Task 07.T09

- [ ] **07.T09.** Add the bounded B41 appearance subset through existing geometry/material/parameter/attachment/variant commands: select a supplied character, expose its declared editable parameters and permitted compatible garments/hair/accessories, and retain source/rig/anchor references. Use inexpensive attached or supplied skinned geometry with validated declared bindings; visual skinning does not start cloth, hair or tissue physics. Keep shared source versus selected-copy edits explicit, support a cheap missing-appearance fallback and retain original source when an arbitrary edit requires the stage 11 rebind/repair path.

